## Fit and metric definitions

[RUN] The sealed fit used the repository `AdamMLPHead` and the exact C2 literals in
`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:44-62`: hidden `(100,50,50)`, tanh, learning rate
`1e-3`, `gauge_beta = 0.1`, Adam `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, and zero weight decay.
Every fold received exactly 2,000 source epochs and one deterministic full-batch update per
epoch. Each fold used the C1REAL construction's deterministic `linspace` cap of 4,096
base-to-candidate pairs.

[RUN] LOAO used the first sealed pilot learner seed (`V025_LEARNER/seed/1`, integer
`6407676579069309528`). LOWO is the arithmetic mean of all four sealed pilot seed metrics;
their individual values and ranges are retained in `results.json`.

[RUN] The plain linear model minimized the same pairwise squared objective plus the C2
`0.1` reference gauge in closed form. The constant used each training fold's mean target.
The modal-floor constant is separately reported so that `−3` cannot masquerade as skill.

[RUN] The high-capacity model was deliberately favorable to C2's known structure. It
computed the exact absorbing penalty from Q2's valid/survival slots, then fit the remaining
forecast surplus with fixed-seed two-layer 256/256 ReLU random features plus all 22 raw
slots and a 535-parameter ridge output. Ridge was selected inside every outer fold using
training-only anchor validation over `{0.01,0.1,1,10,100,1000}`.

[RUN] Metrics are pooled over held-out rows/groups:

- level `R²`: raw predicted level versus normalized target; no test-time re-gauging;
- ordering: every non-tied true action pair within a held-out `(anchor,user)` group;
  prediction ties earn `0.5`;
- top-1: stable predicted argmax is correct when its true target is within `1e-12` of the
  group maximum.

