## What changed and why

### Off-axis angle: repaired at both row paths

[RUN] The two sealed v1 defects are the literal `off_axis_angle_rad=0.0` in the
provider-primitive fallback at
[`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:445`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:445)
and in the exact engine path at
[`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:639`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:639).
The v2 fallback adapter and exact-path adapter are separate entry points at
[`q1_schema_v2.py:452`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:452) and
[`q1_schema_v2.py:464`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:464);
both pass their rows through the same authenticated geometry projection at
[`q1_schema_v2.py:416`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:416).
The sealed builders remain unchanged.

[DERIVED] For satellite position `s`, beam-centre position `c`, and focal-user
position `u`, v2 computes the physical angle at the satellite,

`theta = acos(((c-s) dot (u-s)) / (||c-s|| ||u-s||))`.

This is the same geometry the provider uses to form `direct_angles` before
transmit gain at
[`provider_legacy.py:725`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:725).
The physics helper works in degrees; v2 converts the result to radians because
the inherited Q1 slot contract is radians. The implementation is at
[`q1_schema_v2.py:291`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:291).

[DERIVED] True off-axis is **not** recoverable from a serialized v1 row alone:
the row omits satellite/user/cell ECEF, and the sidelobed Bessel antenna gain is
not a one-to-one inverse for angle. It is recoverable at decision time because
both row builders still have the tape/provider identity and ECEF seams. The v2
resolver uses those exact seams and fails closed when they are absent; it does
not infer angle from gain or substitute elevation as a proxy
([`q1_schema_v2.py:335`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-design-ws/q1_schema_v2.py:335)).

[RUN] Across the full corpus, non-null off-axis spans
`0.0006258963` to `0.1056026098` rad. The all-row minimum is `0` only because
18,000 explicit null-action rows have no focal link. Their geometry is encoded
as `(0,0)` and is gated by the already-authenticated row-level `null_action`
flag; it is not a physical proxy.

### `missing_incumbent`: structurally constant here, not unset

[RUN] Both sealed builders already set the field. The fallback directly uses
`incumbent.mapping[user] is None` at
[`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:454`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:454);
the exact path computes the same predicate at lines 624–625 and emits it at
[`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:656`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:656).

[RUN] Enumeration found `0` missing values in all `176,223` rows and `0`
`None` values in the `18,000` focal incumbent carrier-mapping positions that
generate them. These tapes keep every user served in every fixed-carrier
mapping. At step 0 the builder deliberately uses the current base as the
incumbent; later steps use the preceding carrier mapping. The coordinate is
therefore genuinely structurally constant **on these tapes**.

[INFERRED] V2 retains `missing_incumbent` because the predicate is correctly
implemented and remains meaningful for a successor tape that permits an
unserved prior mapping. Removing it would silently narrow the schema's state
domain. Its corpus-specific constancy and reason are recorded in both the
schema manifest and census.

### Elevation: added in the channel convention

[RUN] `PrimitiveStepArrays` already stores `elevations_deg` on the same rows as
the remaining-time primitives
([`tapes.py:362`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/tapes.py:362)).
V2 adds `focal_link_elevation` in degrees from boundary 0, the same convention
used by the provider/channel. A separate ECEF recomputation agreed with the
stored provider value to a maximum absolute error of
`1.009e-12` degrees over the reconstructed decision geometry. Non-null values
span `13.8129` to `89.6355` degrees.

[DERIVED] The frozen normalization scale is `90 deg`, the physical magnitude
bound of the convention, so this is a unit mapping rather than a tuned value.

[RUN] Elevation and `remaining_visibility_time` have Pearson correlation
`r = 0.930012` over all rows and `r = 0.857463` over non-null links only. The
second number removes the shared `(0,0)` null encoding. Elevation is strongly
related to visibility time, but it is not a duplicate: elevation has `22,991`
distinct corpus values, visibility time has `359`, and elevation's linear
`R^2` on all other v2 slots is `0.894220`, not 1.

### Exact indicator redundancy: dropped explicitly

[RUN] The old corpus again verifies, with zero violations,

- `beam_active_before_focal == 1[background_occupancy_excluding_focal > 0]`;
- `previous_beam_active_for_action == 1[previous_served_load_for_action > 0]`.

[DERIVED] V2 drops the two indicator coordinates because they contain no
information beyond their retained count coordinates. Repairing off-axis and
adding elevation without this choice would have made 17 serialized columns;
dropping the two declared duplicates gives 15. With the one documented
structurally constant coordinate, the effective dimension is `15 - 1 = 14`.
The dimension change is part of the schema payload and therefore part of its
digest.

